## 2. New strategy (rule‑based controller)

```
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
#  Variables (from observation)
#  x  = cart_position          (‑25 … 25)
#  v  = cart_velocity          (‑50 … 50)
#  a  = pole_angle             (‑25 … 25)   // degrees, 0 = upright
#  w  = pole_angular_velocity  (‑50 … 50)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------

IF a >  3            THEN action = 2        # pole leaning right → push right
ELSE IF a < -3      THEN action = 1        # pole leaning left  → push left

ELSE IF w >  3      THEN action = 2        # pole rotating clockwise fast → push right
ELSE IF w < -3      THEN action = 1        # pole rotating counter‑clockwise → push left

ELSE IF x > 15      THEN action = 1        # cart too far right → push left
ELSE IF x < -15     THEN action = 2        # cart too far left  → push right

ELSE IF v > 5       THEN action = 1        # cart moving right fast → push left
ELSE IF v < -5      THEN action = 2        # cart moving left fast  → push right

ELSE                     # everything is near zero
        # move cart toward centre (neutral bias)
        IF x > 0   THEN action = 1
        ELSE IF x < 0 THEN action = 2
        ELSE            action = 2      # arbitrary when perfectly centred
```

### Why this should work better

| Rule | Reason |
|------|--------|
| **Angle ± 3°** | The pole becomes unstable already at a few degrees; correcting earlier avoids the large angular‑velocity build‑up that caused the failure in S‑3. |
| **Angular‑velocity ± 3** | A modest spin indicates the pole is about to diverge; a quick corrective push prevents the angle from crossing the 5° band. |
| **Cart‑position ± 15** | Gives the cart plenty of room (‑25…25) while still pulling it back before it reaches the wall. |
| **Cart‑velocity ± 5** | Dampens drift without fighting the pole‑angle correction; only engages when the cart is gaining speed that could push it into the wall later. |
| **Center‑bias default** | When the system is almost balanced we do not keep pushing in one direction (as S‑3 did with default = 2). The bias gently recenters the cart, preventing a slow drift to one side. |

