| 4 | `[-18, -16, -6, -4]` | Angle = ‑6 → **action = 1** (push left) → same as before, but now the cart has already been nudged toward centre, so it will not stay at –18 for many steps. |
| 9 | `[-20, -22, -1, 4]` | Angle ≈ 0, `w = 4 > 3` → **action = 2** (push right) → cart moves leftward (because right force pushes cart left), pulling the cart back toward centre instead of letting it drift further right. |
| 13‑18 | As the pole angle grows past –3°, the angle rule immediately flips to **action = 1** (push left) and the cart receives a corrective rightward push well before the angle reaches –5°. The pole therefore never reaches the –25° failure limit and the episode can continue far beyond 243 steps. |

