| State | Which clause fires | Action | Why it is better |
|-------|-------------------|--------|------------------|
| `[21 12 1 3]` | Clause 2 (`a>1 && w>0`) → action = 1 (push left) | Left push counters the right‑leaning pole that is also moving right. |
| `[22 9 2 8]` | Clause 2 (`a>1 && w>0`) → action = 1 | Same reasoning – prevents the pole from overshooting. |
| `[23 25 3 ‑15]` | Clause 1 (`a>3`) → action = 1 | Strong angle correction dominates; cart is already far right, but fixing the pole is priority. |
| `[-25 ‑13 ‑3 ‑6]` | Clause 1 (`a<‑3`) → action = 2 (push right) | The pole is falling left while the cart is at the left wall – the rule now pushes right, rescuing the system before failure. |

