2. **Stronger correction when the pole is very close to the failure bound** – if `|a| ≥ 22` we *force* the corrective push **against the direction of the angular velocity** (`sign(w)`) instead of the sign of the angle.  
   At extreme lean the pole’s rotation tells us which way it will fall next; fighting that rotation is more effective than fighting the static lean.

```text
# -------------------------------------------------
#  CART‑POLE BALANCING RULES (integer state)
#  state = [x, v, a, w]   # cart pos, cart vel, pole angle, pole angular vel
#  action = 1 (push left)  or  2 (push right)
# -------------------------------------------------

IF |a| >= 22 THEN                     # pole is almost falling
    IF w > 0 THEN action = 1         # rotating clockwise → push left
    ELSE       action = 2            # rotating counter‑clockwise → push right

ELSE IF |a| >= 4 THEN                  # moderate lean
    IF a > 0 THEN action = 2          # pole leans right → push right
    ELSE       action = 1             # pole leans left  → push left

ELSE IF |w| >= 4 THEN                  # pole nearly upright but spinning
    IF w > 0 THEN action = 2          # clockwise spin → push right
    ELSE       action = 1             # counter‑clockwise → push left

ELSE IF |v| >= 5 THEN                  # cart moving fast, pole safe
    IF v > 0 THEN action = 1          # moving right → push left
    ELSE       action = 2             # moving left  → push right

ELSE IF |x| >= 18 THEN                 # cart far from centre, pole safe
    IF x > 0 THEN action = 1          # too far right → push left
    ELSE       action = 2             # too far left  → push right

ELSE                                   # everything quiet
    # keep previous action (i.e. no new push)
    action = previous_action
# -------------------------------------------------
```

