| Change | Expected effect |
|--------|-----------------|
| **Extreme‑lean → fight rotation** (`|a|≥22` uses `sign(w)`) | Stops the pole from “slipping over” the ±25° limit; the 482‑run often failed exactly when the pole was at ±23° with a large angular velocity. |
| **Higher dead‑zone thresholds** (`|a|≥4`, `|w|≥4`) | Reduces unnecessary jitter when the pole is already near vertical, letting the system coast and therefore keeping the cart more centered. |
| **Neutral default** (keep previous action) | Removes the systematic right‑bias that slowly pushes the cart to the right edge of the track. |
| **Slightly tighter velocity/position limits** (`|v|≥5`, `|x|≥18`) | Gives the controller a chance to recenter the cart *before* the pole angle grows again. |

