## Updated (and now final) rule‑based policy

The policy below is a small refinement of the successful “previous” policy: we keep the same ordering of priorities, tighten the secondary thresholds a little, and add a “center‑cart” fallback that keeps the cart near the middle of the track when everything else is under control.

```
# 1. Correct a large tilt
IF |θ| ≥ 3
    THEN action = LEFT  (1)  IF θ > 0   # pole leans right → move cart left
         ELSE action = RIGHT (2)      # pole leans left  → move cart right

# 2. Counter a fast rotation (only when tilt is already small)
ELSE IF |ω| ≥ 2
    THEN action = LEFT  (1)  IF ω > 0   # pole rotating clockwise → move cart left
