**What worked and what didn’t**

* **Assumption 1 – “Angle dominates”** – true when |θ| ≥ 3. The pole is far from vertical and a force in the direction of the lean is the fastest way to bring it back.
* **Assumption 2 – “When angle is small, use angular velocity”** – also true. If we ignore ω the pole can start rotating away from the vertical even though |θ| < 3.
