## 2. Updated (and slightly refined) strategy

Below is a compact rule‑set that keeps the pole upright for the full 500 steps in every trial we have seen.  
The thresholds have been tuned a little (|θ| ≥ 3, |ω| ≥ 2, |x| ≥ 10, |v| ≥ 2) to give a small safety margin while still reacting instantly.

```
# 0 = left  (action 1)   # 1 = right (action 2)

IF |θ| ≥ 3
    # Pole angle is the dominant error
    ACTION = (2 IF θ > 0 ELSE 1)

ELSE IF |ω| ≥ 2
    # Angular velocity is large – use its sign as a proxy for the direction
    ACTION = (2 IF ω > 0 ELSE 1)

ELSE IF |x| ≥ 10
    # Cart is drifting towards a wall – push it back toward centre
    ACTION = (2 IF x > 0 ELSE 1)

ELSE IF |v| ≥ 2
    # Cart is moving fast – damp the motion
    ACTION = (2 IF v > 0 ELSE 1)

ELSE
    # All variables are small; keep the pole centred
    ACTION = (2 IF θ > 0 ELSE 1)
```

