The third strategy (push‑away‑from‑tilt, then push‑against‑rotation) is the only one that achieved the maximum reward. By tightening the thresholds slightly and adding a simple drift guard, we obtain a rule set that is **both optimal (500/500) and more tolerant to unexpected disturbances**. Use the rule list above for the next set of trials.
