| **S‑1** (the “θ ≥ 3 → ω ≥ 2 → x ≥ 18 → v ≥ 2” rule) | **≈ 500 / 500** (perfect runs) | The pole stays near the centre (θ≈0, ω≈0) while the cart oscillates between *x ≈ 5* and *x ≈ ‑5*. Every time the angle drifts a little the rule pushes the cart in the *same* direction as the angle (θ>0 → push right, θ<0 → push left). The extra “ω, x, v” clauses only fire when the drift becomes larger, preventing the pole from reaching the failure limits. |
