* **Magnitude‑aware thresholds** – stronger pushes when the pole is far from vertical.  
* **Coupled angle/velocity decision** – when |θ| is large *and* ω has the same sign as θ, push **against** the angle (i.e. apply a “braking” force) to reduce angular momentum before the pole crosses the safety bound.  
