### 2. Updated rule set (the “best‑of‑both‑worlds” controller)

Below is a compact, easy‑to‑read rule table that reproduces the behaviour of Strategy C, but adds a few safety checks that were missing in the earlier attempts.

```
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# 1️⃣  Strong tilt → push toward the tilt (restoring torque)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
IF |θ| >= 3
    ACTION = 2  IF θ > 0      # pole leaning right → push right
    ACTION = 1  IF θ < 0      # pole leaning left  → push left

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# 2️⃣  Small tilt but fast spin → push in direction of spin
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
ELSE IF |ω| >= 2
    ACTION = 2  IF ω > 0      # pole rotating counter‑clockwise → push right
    ACTION = 1  IF ω < 0      # pole rotating clockwise        → push left

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# 3️⃣  Cart drifting toward a wall (but pole still safe) → recenter
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
ELSE IF |x| >= 18
    ACTION = 1  IF x > 0      # cart too far right → push left
    ACTION = 2  IF x < 0      # cart too far left  → push right

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# 4️⃣  Cart moving fast while pole is near vertical → brake
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
ELSE IF |v| >= 4
    ACTION = 1  IF v > 0      # moving right fast → push left
    ACTION = 2  IF v < 0      # moving left  fast → push right

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# 5️⃣  Default (everything almost balanced) → keep pole on the
#      side it is already leaning – this avoids unnecessary jitter.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
ELSE
    ACTION = 2  IF θ > 0
    ACTION = 1  IF θ < 0
