| **4) |x| ≥ 20** | If the cart wanders close to the edge of the allowed region we nudge it further outward **without** trying to recenter it aggressively. This mirrors the behaviour of the perfect runs (cart stayed around x ≈ 9). |
| **5) |v| ≥ 3** | Damps large cart speeds that could later cause overshoot. The value 3 is lower than the 2 used previously because we now have a stronger angle‑driven controller; a smaller velocity threshold gives a smoother motion. |
| **6) Default** | When everything is small we simply choose a deterministic action (right). Any constant works; the policy will immediately react as soon as the pole deviates. |

