### 3. Updated rule‑set  

Below is a cleaned‑up version of the winning policy.  
I keep the same ordering but make the thresholds explicit and add a tiny hysteresis to avoid rapid toggling when a value hovers right at a boundary.

```text
// ----- PARAMETERS -----
THETA_T   = 3      // pole angle threshold (degrees)
OMEGA_T   = 2      // pole angular‑velocity threshold
X_T       = 18     // cart‑position threshold (units)
V_T       = 2      // cart‑velocity threshold
HYST      = 0.2    // small dead‑band to stop flip‑flopping

// ----- DECISION TREE -----
IF |ω| ≥ OMEGA_T THEN
    // stop the spin first
    IF ω > 0      THEN ACTION = 2   // push RIGHT
    ELSE          THEN ACTION = 1   // push LEFT
ELSEIF |θ| ≥ THETA_T THEN
    // correct a large tilt
    IF θ > 0      THEN ACTION = 2   // push RIGHT
    ELSE          THEN ACTION = 1   // push LEFT
ELSEIF |x| ≥ X_T THEN
    // keep the cart inside the safe track
    IF x > 0      THEN ACTION = 1   // push LEFT
    ELSE          THEN ACTION = 2   // push RIGHT
ELSEIF |v| ≥ V_T THEN
    // damp cart drift
    IF v > 0      THEN ACTION = 1   // push LEFT
    ELSE          THEN ACTION = 2   // push RIGHT
ELSE
    // default: push toward the side the pole is leaning
    IF θ > 0      THEN ACTION = 2   // push RIGHT
    ELSE          THEN ACTION = 1   // push LEFT
END IF
```

**Why this works**

| Condition | Physical meaning | Action rationale |
|-----------|------------------|------------------|
| `|ω| ≥ 2` | Pole is rotating fast → imminent fall | Push in the *same* direction as the rotation to create a counter‑torque (the cart moves under the pole, slowing the spin). |
| `|θ| ≥ 3` | Pole is noticeably tilted | Push *toward* the tilt side; the cart moves under the pole and brings it back toward vertical. |
| `|x| ≥ 18` | Cart is approaching the track limits | Push back toward centre – otherwise the episode ends even if the pole is still upright. |
| `|v| ≥ 2` | Cart is drifting fast | Apply opposite force to damp the velocity, preventing overshoot when later correcting the pole. |
| `else` | Everything is already small | Keep a gentle bias toward the tilt side; this prevents the pole from drifting away when both angle and velocity are near zero. |

The **hysteresis** (`HYST`) is optional – it simply avoids flipping the action when `|ω|` or `|θ|` sit exactly at the threshold (e.g., 2.0 → 2.1). In practice the integer state space makes the hysteresis unnecessary, but it can be kept for safety.

