   When |ω| ≥ 2 the correct corrective action is **the same direction as the pole’s angular velocity** (i.e. if the pole is rotating clockwise (ω > 0) we must push the cart **right** (action 2) to create a counter‑clockwise torque). The successful strategy (A) uses this sign, while the failing ones use the opposite sign.

2. **Cart‑position and cart‑velocity rules should oppose the drift.**  
   - If the cart is far right (x > 0) we must push **left** (action 1) to bring it back.  
   - If the cart is moving right (v > 0) we also push **left**.  
   The opposite sign (pushing further away) short‑circuits the stabilisation and leads to early failures.

3. **When everything is small (|θ|, |ω|, |x|, |v| < thresholds) the safest default is to keep pushing **away from the pole angle** (i.e. the same rule as the first line).**  
